From d200c7f093ccd78ccf57f5e505dd73410ba46491 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:37:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs(r52b): re-point the two test-case-list citations that
 this lane's own comment growth shifted
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to 41b808eab, which closed the PASS-GATED docs gate. Correcting F1's
overstatement expanded both lane-243 comment blocks in tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
(eval 6 -> 10 lines, perf 4 -> 6), which pushed the rows below them down. The report
still cited the pre-expansion ranges :10768-10777 and :12042-12049 — the same species
of stale citation the parent commit fixed for :9923-9929, introduced by the fix itself.

Report §1 and §4.1 now cite :10768-10780 (eval) and :12046-12054 (perf), stated as
"as of this commit", with the instruction to find the blocks by their `lane-243 / R52b`
marker rather than by line number, since any further edit moves them again.

Also in the perf comment: "the bs loop above" was imprecise — the {1,2,3,4,5,8,512} x
all_types loop that already timed SX8 at 4096x14336 n=512 is an earlier loop, not the
block immediately above the new rows. Reworded, same line count.

Also closes the last clause of check F1: report §1 now states that the commit messages
of a63edc326, e67997dc8 and 4f794ab3f carry the same overstatement and that §1 is the
correction of record for all three — history is not rewritten for a wording defect.

The .cpp edit is comment text only; the diff is zero-behaviour.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-243 R52b docs gate, Opus 5 MEDIUM docs-maker)
Measured-effect: none - documentation only
Lane: lane-243
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 OPUS-R52B-SX8-COOPMAT-MULMM-REPORT.md | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp            | 10 +++++-----
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp b/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
index 7cfcb2b78..afb80a1f0 100644
--- a/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
+++ b/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
@@ -12044,11 +12044,11 @@ static std::vector<std::unique_ptr<test_case>> make_test_cases_perf() {
     }
 
     // ArifiLabs lane-243 / R52b: the PREFILL width on the 27B FFN SHAPE, which perf mode did not
-    // have. Perf mode DID already time S-X8 mul_mm: the bs loop above runs {1,2,3,4,5,8,512} over
-    // all_types, and all_types contains GGML_TYPE_SX8, so 4096x14336 at n=512 was already a timed
-    // mul_mm row. What was missing is this shape -- m = 17408, k = 5120 -- the row the R52b pairing
-    // is quoted on. q8_0 is the paired control. The eval list carries the same two rows as
-    // CORRECTNESS cases.
+    // have. Perf mode DID already time S-X8 mul_mm: an EARLIER bs loop (not the block immediately
+    // above) runs {1,2,3,4,5,8,512} over all_types, which contains GGML_TYPE_SX8, so 4096x14336 at
+    // n=512 was already a timed mul_mm row. What was missing is THIS shape -- m = 17408, k = 5120,
+    // the row the R52b pairing is quoted on. q8_0 is the paired control. The eval list carries the
+    // same two rows as CORRECTNESS cases.
     for (ggml_type type_a : {GGML_TYPE_SX8, GGML_TYPE_Q8_0}) {
         test_cases.emplace_back(new test_mul_mat(type_a, GGML_TYPE_F32, 17408, 512, 5120, {1, 1}, {1, 1}));
     }
